 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Most people just toss it down hole each night. Then double it with a hose leak repair foam before going. It' worth it for the small footprint. Bury them under a thin layer of dirt each night. They' last for several nights before someone steps on one and it pops. It's to keep the site tidy and prevent access. Most sites have them as rules, so it' worth following them. You've already beat the two biggest ones. Tossing waste down hole each night and burying food scraps. Now you' a pro.",
